  <diagram id="p8" name="8 · How skills point at each other">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1278" pageHeight="2098" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="note" value="Page 8 — how skill files point at each other, by FORM.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Since ROADMAP 73 (n), 2026-10-12, a pointer is a relative Markdown link whose visible text is the old name form: 4571 of 4748 skill-name and rules/NN pointers are links (3938 of the 4056 that name a rules file). The unlinked rest are mostly bare prose mentions of a skill. 1704 mentions of another skill&#x27;s name across 348 skill files; 3 @path tokens, all in sota-docs-workflow/rules/01-documentation-architecture.md, which DESCRIBES the CLAUDE.md feature.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Why links: with names only, an agent had to turn the name into a directory and the number into a file, and every failed rules-file read in sota-agent-evals v6-v11 was a guessed filename. Measured in v12: links ended the guessing (failed reads 2 -&gt; 0) but did NOT raise how often the cited rules file was reached (5/20 names, 6/20 links): agents follow the links where they sit, not to the file the task needs. A hook naming the file for the code being written reached 18/20 (v9)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1100" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
